{
    "$schema": "https://go.kicad.org/pcm/schemas/v2",
    "name": "Tracklayer autorouter",
    "description": "Autoroute the open board: exact-geometry (shape) or grid engine, any number of copper layers.",
    "description_full": "Tracklayer routes the unrouted nets of the open board and adds the tracks and vias as one undoable change, then refills the zones. The shape engine works on exact geometry: every obstacle is grown by the clearance plus half the track width and tracks run corner to corner, so clearances are met exactly and tight escapes from fine-pitch pads just work. The grid engine gives classic 45-degree tracks. Net classes, locked and hand-routed copper, keep-outs and pours are respected. Any number of copper layers with through vias.\n\nTools > External Plugins > Tracklayer autoroute. Pure Python. Runs through the KiCad API: enable it once under Preferences > Plugins > Enable KiCad API.\n\nMade by Tiggy Engineering (www.tiggyengineering.com). Free and open source; if it saves you an evening, have a look at what we make, or buy us a beer through GitHub Sponsors: github.com/sponsors/MichaelGaylor",
